<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mikatagahara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1573">1573</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mikatagahara was fought on 25 January 1573 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamamatsu">Hamamatsu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/totomi-province">Tōtōmi Province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a>, advancing west, crushed the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> and his Oda allies, and Ieyasu barely escaped to Hamamatsu Castle. Shingen's death a few months later halted the Takeda advance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mikatagahara.jpg" alt="Battle of Mikatagahara" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Yoshitora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Mikatagahara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
